An X11 window's state (Task 33 of docs/plans/20261014-gpui-frontend.md). GPUI reads an X11 window's
`_NET_WM_STATE_HIDDEN`, which a window manager sets on an iconified window, but keeps it to itself, and `window.list`
reports `minimized` from it as the GTK build reads GDK's minimized state there; GPUI's `is_maximized` reads false while
the window is minimized, though the window manager keeps it maximized, and the frame saved at a quit needs that. The X11
client notes both each time it reads the window's `_NET_WM_STATE` and forgets the window when it goes;
`gpui_linux::x11_window_minimized` and `gpui_linux::x11_window_maximized` read them by the window's X id. And a
`Blurred` background asks KWin's blur behind the window on X11 (`_KDE_NET_WM_BLUR_BEHIND_REGION`, an empty region:
the whole window), as GPUI's Wayland backend asks `org_kde_kwin_blur`; before, X11 took `Blurred` as `Transparent`.
Wayland (whose xdg-shell has no minimized state) and the other platforms are unchanged. scripts/vendor-gpui.sh applies
this to the verified crates.io archive.

